{"page":1,"totalPages":3,"perPage":6,"nextPage":2,"html":"<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/molecule-builder.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/molecule-builder.webp\" alt=\"Sulfur dioxide in 3D: a yellow sulfur nucleus bent between two red oxygens, each joined by a pair of cylinders for the double bond, with a pale blue lone-pair lobe rising from the sulfur\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>11 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/molecule-builder\">Building molecules out of two rules</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Drop atoms into a 3D workspace, bond them together, and watch the geometry arrange itself. Methane finds its tetrahedron, benzene flattens into a hexagon, water bends to 104.5° — from two rules, one fitted number, and no table of angles.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Chemistry</li><li>3D</li><li>Javascript</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/tree-lab.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/tree-lab.webp\" alt=\"A Red-Black tree simulation mid-repair, with the rotation being narrated underneath\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>10 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/self-balancing-trees\">Four ways to keep a tree balanced</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A search tree is only fast while it stays short, and there are surprisingly different ways to keep it that way: measure heights, colour nodes, roll dice, or give up on binary altogether. Add and delete values in all four and watch each one repair itself a step at a time.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Data Structures</li><li>Balanced Binary Tree</li><li>AVL</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/shape-playground.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/shape-playground.webp\" alt=\"A translucent icosidodecahedron in 3D: green triangles and amber pentagons over a cage of edges, with a pale sphere at each of its thirty vertices\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>15 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/shape-playground\">The solids that two forces can find, and the ones they cannot</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Drop charged vertices into a 3D workspace, join them, and let them settle. Every Platonic solid comes out with its edges equal to within a thousandth, from an energy that has no notion of an angle and no rest length. The Archimedean solids come out wrong, and the reason why turns out to be the interesting part.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Geometry</li><li>3D</li><li>Javascript</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/tree-game.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/tree-game.webp\" alt=\"The tree sequence playground, showing an illegal move with the embedded earlier tree ringed\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>7 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/tree-sequence-game\">The game behind TREE(3)</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Two rules, a handful of coloured dots, and a longest game so vast that with three colours nobody can write the answer down. Build sequences here and let the computer tell you the moment you break the rules.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Mathematics</li><li>Logic</li><li>Trees</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/watch-movement.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/watch-movement.webp\" alt=\"A close-up of the escapement: a gilt balance wheel with timing screws around its rim and a blued hairspring coiled inside it, the steel pallet fork beside it, and the escape wheel and fourth wheel to the right, with the rest of the movement faded to a ghost behind them\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>15 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/watch-movement\">A watch that is not animated</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">The seconds hand moves because a balance wheel is vibrating, and for no other reason. Wind the crown, pull it out to set the time, and fade the bridges away to watch the escapement lock, unlock and impulse five times a second.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Horology</li><li>3D</li><li>Javascript</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/solar-eclipses.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/solar-eclipses.webp\" alt=\"The solar eclipse app showing an annular eclipse shadow crossing South America\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-03-22T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.03.22</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/solar-eclipses\">Visualizing solar eclipses</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A total eclipse is a cosmic coincidence: a moon that just barely covers the sun. This app lets you move through the Sun, Moon and Earth system and watch the geometry that decides which patch of the planet falls into shadow.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>Visualization</li><li>Astronomy</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>"}